Goal: Build a small API that stores nothing. No database, no arrays or variables that keep data between requests. Every response is worked out from the request itself.
1. Basic routing
• GET / returns { message: "Toolbox API" }
• GET /greet/:name?lang=en|id returns "Hello, Manu" or "Halo, Manu"
Tests: path params, query, simple responses
2. Validation with t
• POST /bmi takes { weight: number, height: number } (both must be more than 0) and returns the BMI and its category
• GET /convert/temperature?value=30&from=c&to=f where from and to can only be c, f or k
Tests: t.Object, t.Number, t.Union / t.Literal, and the automatic 422 error when input is wrong
3. Groups and plugins
• Put the text routes in a separate file as a plugin and add it with .use()
• Group them under /text:
    ◦ POST /text/count returns how many characters, words and vowels the text has
    ◦ POST /text/reverse returns the text reversed
    ◦ POST /text/slug turns "Hello World!" into "hello-world"
Tests: new Elysia({ prefix }), .group(), .use()
4. Lifecycle hooks
• Use derive to give each request a requestId and a start time
• Use onAfterHandle to add X-Request-Id and X-Response-Time headers to every response
• Use onRequest to log the method and URL
Tests: derive, the lifecycle order, setting headers
5. Guard
• Under /secure/*, require the header x-api-key: secret123. Without it, return 401.
• GET /secure/time returns the server time
Tests: .guard(), beforeHandle, header validation
6. Error handling
• Make a custom DivisionByZeroError
• GET /math/divide?a=10&b=0 throws it
• Use onError so every error comes back in one format: { error: string, code: string }
Tests: error() / status(), custom errors, onError
7. Docs and tests
• Add the OpenAPI plugin and check that /openapi shows every route
• Write bun:test tests for at least 5 routes, using app.handle(new Request(...)) or Eden Treaty
Bonus
• WS /ws/echo: a WebSocket that sends back each message in uppercase
• Use Eden Treaty to call the API with full types
What to submit
• The source code, with the plugin in its own file
• Passing tests (bun test)
